            "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Garenburg Woods is a happy RPG game made in RPG Maker 2000. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Welcome to Garenburg Woods!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Egly is going on a trip with his friends, Elfy, Carib, Yhien, and Malik. The friends are heading over to the Garenburg Cliffs, a wonderful place that is said to have a beautiful sight. Everybody is sure to have a great time... </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Turn-based combat system </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An original soundtrack </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A story filled with lore and secrets </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Over 10 different bosses to fight </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Three main endings </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >RISK Mode: limited saves, harder boss fights, more secrets, and risky items only that will decrease stats or improve your strength </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Happy Mode: extremely overpowered and for those who want to play purely for plot</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Numerous party members with unique abilities to populate your team </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Numerous achievements to unlock</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Plenty of secrets to find and areas to explore</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Stay on trail  </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dolls and puppets </p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Average Playthrough Length</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >These are estimates and can vary for your actual playthrough and if you know what you're doing. Your time could differ from this.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Ignoring things and just trying to get by as quickly as possible - 30 minutes to 2 hours </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Exploring and finding around half of the content - 1-3 hours </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Getting the true ending and main content events - 2-6 hours</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Be happy.</p>",
            "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Garenburg Woods is a happy RPG game made in RPG Maker 2000. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Welcome to Garenburg Woods!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Egly is going on a trip with his friends, Elfy, Carib, Yhien, and Malik. The friends are heading over to the Garenburg Cliffs, a wonderful place that is said to have a beautiful sight. Everybody is sure to have a great time... </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Turn-based combat system </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An original soundtrack </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A story filled with lore and secrets </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Over 10 different bosses to fight </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Three main endings </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >RISK Mode: limited saves, harder boss fights, more secrets, and risky items only that will decrease stats or improve your strength </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Happy Mode: extremely overpowered and for those who want to play purely for plot</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Numerous party members with unique abilities to populate your team </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Numerous achievements to unlock</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Plenty of secrets to find and areas to explore</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Stay on trail  </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dolls and puppets </p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Average Playthrough Length</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >These are estimates and can vary for your actual playthrough and if you know what you're doing. Your time could differ from this.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Ignoring things and just trying to get by as quickly as possible - 30 minutes to 2 hours </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Exploring and finding around half of the content - 1-3 hours </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Getting the true ending and main content events - 2-6 hours</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Be happy.</p>",
